# Groomer portal env (copy to .env.local)

# Groomer backend base URL used by the API client (via the Vite /api proxy by default).
# The groomer backend is structurally identical to the vet backend (same routes.rs contracts).
VITE_GROOMER_API_BASE=/api

# Central admin API base — the whitelist-apply posts issuer-applications here.
VITE_CENTRAL_API_BASE=http://localhost:39742

# Dev proxy target for /api (the groomer backend). Defaults to http://localhost:43618.
VITE_GROOMER_API_PROXY=http://localhost:43618

# Reown Cloud projectId for WalletConnect (REQUIRED for real wallet-connect).
# A placeholder is used if unset; WalletConnect transport will not function until set.
VITE_REOWN_PROJECT_ID=REPLACE_WITH_REOWN_PROJECT_ID

# Optional: the deployment URL shown in share/verify QR captions.
VITE_DEPLOYMENT_URL=http://localhost:43617

# Guarded default ROAX RPC + deployed contract addresses (contracts/deployments/roax.json). Users
# may save another same-chain peer in Settings; a bad custom peer falls back to this independently
# guarded default. This changes direct reads only, never the central/indexer APIs or the provider
# used by an injected/WalletConnect wallet for transactions. The issue-status panel polls
# DogTagIssuer.isValid(merkleRoot) via viem to surface "Verified on-chain". In wallet mode the issuer
# address comes from the prepare response (unsignedTx.to); in backend mode set
# VITE_DOGTAG_ISSUER_ADDR to the per-recordType DogTagIssuer to enable live polling.
VITE_ROAX_RPC=https://devrpc.roax.net
VITE_DOGTAG_ISSUER_ADDR=
VITE_ISSUER_REGISTRY_ADDR=0xAEE540350292E49A9AeDf19Dd4C3BAc6ABeE6c21

# ---- GENERATION 2 — NOT DEPLOYED, so DELIBERATELY UNSET ---------------------------------------
# The key above is what MOVES in the cutover. Its NAME does not change; only its VALUE does, so there
# is deliberately nothing to add below: an extra variable here, empty or otherwise, would be config
# nothing reads, and a placeholder address would be worse than an absent one.
# S-13 repoints; S-14 deploys and records the addresses in contracts/deployments/roax.json.
#
#   VITE_ISSUER_REGISTRY_ADDR  -> DOES NOT MOVE AT C-9  (BLOCKED - see below)
#
# It moves IN STEP with this stack's backend ISSUER_REGISTRY_ADDR (../.env) - and that variable is
# BLOCKED, so this one is too. ProviderRegistry.isWhitelistedFor branches on msg.sender, and this read
# passes no account, so msg.sender is 0x0 and it answers the orthogonal VERIFY-key capability instead
# of the issuance whitelist. This portal asks with recordTypeKey(...), which is never a VERIFY key, so
# every row would render false. The backend is blocked for its own reasons (see ../.env.example). The
# unblock is the isRecognizedIssuer(service, signer) migration (docs/ISSUER_V2_OWNERSHIP.md #8).
#
# The governing condition: an address may be repointed only when the successor answers THE SAME
# QUESTION FOR THE SAME INPUTS. A matching selector is not evidence of that, and here the call
# SUCCEEDS and returns a well-typed, confidently wrong answer.
#
# Inventory + checker: scripts/check-cutover-consumers.sh. Full record: docs/CLIENT_REPOINT.md.

# Demo mode (default OFF). When set to 1 (or "true"), the portal prefills forms, shows
# "Fill demo data" buttons (a parenthesised variant where a form offers several presets, e.g.
# "Fill demo data (vet)"), and autofills the demo admin password /
# passphrase. NEVER enable in production — in demo mode the vet genesis seed is briefly stashed
# in sessionStorage to auto-fill the confirm step. Unset = secure production behavior.
# VITE_DEMO_MODE=1
